ntly clobbers\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: cef69ec2-8b5a-4e91-8078-ac955e039295\n  modified: 2026-07-29T03:59:46.408Z\n---\n\nShipped 0.14.0 (on main). Push now carries only the anchors a read at that rev\nresolves to; storage unchanged.\n\n**The framing that unlocked it** (user's, 2026-07-27): three layers each need a\ngranularity — storage is per-commit, reads are per-branch, push was per-*ref*\ni.e. per-repo. Push was the only one out of step. Not a storage problem.\n\n**No mapping is persisted.** Reachability is recomputed from the DAG at push\ntime (`resolveAnchors`), same reason reads never stored it. Branch membership\nis derived; a stored copy needs maintaining through merge/rebase/rename/delete.\n\n**Two gotchas, each pinned by a test proven to fail against the wrong version:**\n\n1. *Scope must resolve `re_anchor`*, not just `git rev-list`. A squash merge\n   leaves conversations on anchors unreachable from the target; only mapping\n   events (anchored to the survivor) tie them back. Rev-list-only would push\n   the mappings and strand the events.\n2. *A scoped push must seed from the remote's tip and union into it.* A notes\n   ref is a snapshot of the whole database, not an append log — pushing a\n   filtered tree still fast-forwards while deleting every other branch's notes\n   from the remote's current view. Note the *unseeded* naive version is\n   harmless (non-FF rejection); it's the realistic \"filter my local ref\"\n   version that clobbers.\n\n**Side benefit:** the pre-push scan gate now only inspects in-scope events, so\nan out-of-scope finding no longer blocks unrelated pushes.\n\n**Known limitation:** the pre-push hook uses `</dev/null`, so it scopes by HEAD\nrather than the refs git is pushing. Pushing a branch you aren't on\nunder-sends (safe direction); next sync from that branch ships it.\n\n**Still open:** `readEvents`/`export` default to unscoped — the read half of\nthe same mismatch. Fix belongs in `readEvents`, since library consumers\n(intent-recall) never touch the CLI.\n\nSee [[project-cledger-worktree-gitdir]], [[project-ledger-ecosystem]].\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-push-scope.md","memdirStamped":true,"originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"ada4de96-41bb-4f17-bb55-85a83976eb2b","version":"2.1.220"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-07-29T04:00:14.453Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
